{
  "note": "Synthetic. Shape follows Z.ai's documented quota/limit payload, including the two TOKENS_LIMIT rows that differ only by unit. Every value is invented. The credit-tier case follows ClaudeBar's ZaiUsageProbe, which maps CREDIT_LIMIT to the same windows as TOKENS_LIMIT for plans that bill in credits. Every value is invented. One case added 2026-09-27 from a probe with an invalid token: this endpoint reports a rejected credential in the body with an HTTP 200, so UsageHTTP's 401 handling never fires. The values are the service's own error shape and carry no account data.",
  "verifiedAt": "2026-09-20",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a full report",
      "response": {
        "data": {
          "limits": [
            {
              "type": "TOKENS_LIMIT",
              "unit": 3,
              "percentage": 65,
              "nextResetTime": "2026-09-20T20:00:00Z"
            },
            {
              "type": "TOKENS_LIMIT",
              "unit": 6,
              "percentage": 41.5,
              "nextResetTime": "2026-09-24T00:00:00Z"
            },
            {
              "type": "TIME_LIMIT",
              "unit": 5,
              "percentage": 12,
              "nextResetTime": "2026-09-20T20:00:00Z"
            },
            {
              "type": "UNKNOWN_LIMIT",
              "unit": 99,
              "percentage": 100,
              "nextResetTime": "2026-09-20T20:00:00Z"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "gauges": [
          {
            "id": "TOKENS_LIMIT-3",
            "badge": "5H",
